\f1\fs22 Alexander always grew impatient with the mundane set-up before a show. There was not an excuse to run a camera anywhere. And his thoughts were full of Sarah. He couldn\'92t stop picturing her, a modern blonde Holy Mary Madonna with great calves, beautiful and radiant as she selected the cocktail dress and accessories she\'92d wear for the birth of her own baby Alexander Jesus.\
He called the carpool and arranged for a limo with the best new car smell to come pick him up. A few minutes later he was standing across the circuit from Sarah\'92s townhouse.\
\'93Nice one, mother,\'94 he said to himself as he regarded the security detail protecting Sarah\'92s front door. Eloise had obviously responded to the Elvi hordes roaming the streets, and there was no way the UDF could be trusted to keep them under control.\
Alexander practised his strolling as he crossed the street and walked up the path. \'93Afternoon, boys,\'94 he said to the pair of Shakti security protecting his Sarah.\
The pair blocked Alexander and stood to attention.\
\'93We were not informed of your arrival, Mr Shakti,\'94 one of them said, his voice trembling.\
\'93I\'92m recently back from business in Europe, and I\'92m here to see my wife,\'94 Alexander said, careful to keep an air of command out of his voice.\
\'93We\'92ve had orders to let not one pass, sir.\'94\
Alexander looked them over, then glanced at his watch. \'93Look, I\'92m due in make-up shortly\'85 the show is broadcasting live from six.\'94\
The guards trembled, and one of them broke. \'93You\'92re filming an ep of Candid Criminal here, sir?\'94\
\'93Yes. Possibly the last one ever. We\'92re shooting from the Lysander.\'94 Alexander paused, looked back to the street for a moment, then turned his best smile on the guards. \'93Look, it\'92s a closed set\'97sensitive special guest and all that, but I guess I could smuggle you in, if you\'92d like to see how the sausage is executed.\'94\
\'93Oh, I\'92m a big fan, sir. A big fan.\'94\
\'93Really?\'94 Alexander smiled and his lungs filled with proud air. \'93What\'92s your favourite ep?\'94\
\'93Season five, episode thirteen.\'94\
Alexander thought for a bit. \'93Oh yes, the indigenous rights activist faking cerebral palsy.\'94\
\'93I thought strapping him in to his wheelchair for the trebuchet slap was inspired television, sir.\'94\
Alexander waved his finger. \'93You know, we had no idea how the wheelchair would fail when it hit the concrete, but I think you would agree the results were quite\'85\'94\
\'93Memorable, sir, it was memorable.\'94\
\'93Yes. That was the first episode we ran long on. There was just no way we could, in good conscience, edit it any tighter than we did.\'94\
\'93Oh, I agree sir.\'94\
\'93I\'92m glad you appreciate the visual arts, soldier.\'94\
Both security guards beamed.\
\'93Now, look. I must confess I slipped back into the country unannounced. My own mother was surprised\'97and overjoyed\'97to see me. I\'92m sure she\'92s just been too busy to notify you of my arrival.\'94\
\'93Yes, sir. Very good, sir.\'94\
The guards stepped aside.\
Alexander went through the door and down the hall, savouring the prospect of being reunited with his trophy-beautiful other half. He found Sarah slumped in a sofa in the family room.\
\'93Alexander!\'94 \
Sarah appeared so alarmed, Alexander looked over his shoulder for danger. \'93Sarah?\'94\
The woman in the sofa tried to lift herself off the sofa with the grace of a walrus with no sense of balance. Alexander stuttered. \'93You\'92re so\'85\'94\
The woman wobbled on her feet. \'93Pregnant?\'94\
\'93What has mother done to you?\'94 Alexander catalogued the deprivations. Eloise must have denied Sarah her wardrobe, her make-up and her hairdresser. And probably her exercise bike, judging by her calves.\
\'93I\'92m under house arrest, Alexander. And I\'92ve been a damn fool.\'94\
\'93You look so\'85\'94\
\'93Pregnant?\'94\
\'93I was going to say tired.\'94\
Sarah slumped and supported her back with her right hand. \'93That I am.\'94 She made her way to the kitchen and drew a glass of water from the tap. \'93Alexander?\'94\
\'93Yes, my tender walrus.\'94\
\'93If you\'92ve ever been in love with the idea of being in love with me, here\'92s what I need you to do.\'94\
Alexander\'92s eyes misted over. \'93Of course, Sarah, I\'92d do anything for you. Just fix your hair.\'94
